        {
            "block_label": "image",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"imgs/img_in_image_box_149_179_1057_517.jpg\" alt=\"Image\" width=\"74%\" />\n\n(a) GROUND THE PUZZLE\nEmpirical relevance before abstraction\n- 0 Research Intake\nEvidence, intuition, context\n- Refine\n- 1 Puzzle Refinement\nMechanism-focused research question\nHIL-1 - accept puzzle\n- Position\n- 2 Literature Positioning\nNovelty risk & theory neighborhood\nHIL-2 - accept positioning\n- Reality, check\n- 2a Empirical Reality Check\nTest market, institution, and group\nassumptions\n- Gate 1b - Reality Fit PASS / REFRAME / REROUTE\nReality claims are checked before the model structure is fixed.\n(b) CONSTRUCT THE MODEL\nCanonical lineage before novelty claims\n- 3 • 3b Persons Council → Canonical Matching\nMechanism-Math - Positioning - Skeptic\nHIL-3 - accept council synthesis\n- Model Library general - DSE TO - trade - labor\n- Match\n- 4 Model Primitives\nAgents - timing - information equilibrium\nHIL-4 - EQUILIBRIUM HARD STOP\nAudit\n- 5 Assumption Audit\nClosure, coherence, necessity, transparency\nThe agent extends a theoretical lineage; it does not invent a model from scratch.\n(c) STRESS-TEST AND INTERPRET\nFormal, numerical, and economic scrutiny\n- 6 Proposition Generator\nHIL-5 - select\n- 7 Proof Sketch\nDerivative\n- 8 Proof Sketch\n- 9 Economic Interpretation\nMechanism, welfare, empirical implications\nGate 5\nGate 6 math review\nLaTeX → PDF\n\n</div>\n",
